{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is right-angled at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and the semicircle has diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/164abb6bd18d06bfe942472fac852a1df64b2f0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b1538c699086e13a23ff9107282fc46ec50a072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, what is the area of the semi-circle? \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/1/94110c134bd14c0d25a0ca76e48558841f602ef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 37.5\\pi  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 75\\pi  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 100\\pi  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 150\\pi  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 225\\pi  \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"526\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a>, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af03560fe12f82b75ad7c46d0bee180cf2f2ae4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^{2} + BC^{2} = AC^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86ae61c20806bdf67f906799b7aae1fb19a8900b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^{2} + BC^{2} + 40^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/a/b5a3d1ae07f3f49a16ecb927ebde30abd95a0a6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC^{2} + 400 = 1600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb292c08e5fd837176f00d9f4fda2ea16e918d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC^{2} = 1600 - 400 = 1200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"209\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This would be the square of the diameter of the semicircle, so the square of the radius would be:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/681937f18776977c357a1c966eb7d6215346be21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{BC}{2})^{2} = \\frac{BC^{2}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"121\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d0c8fe8f6791b9d3ea77df87061c6370947a0c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{1200}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/663b9fba3a7fadb7edac9e259fc0a48a4a245db9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The area of a semicircle is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec1756c4f77872fac54245ba3ab8c4c831df0dbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi r^{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"41\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the radius of the semicircle. Thus, the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/5/be574bfe4f35477f9c35d2e251931573d5b48733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi \\times 300}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51a1659f58820629c9898a2a2f7f464125e26291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 150\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"87\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a h